Game Dev General Paths
Design
The overall designers, big thinkers of the project. They have to be well rounded in all the disciplines to understand how all the parts of the team move together, and have to have a good vision of the game

Programming
Have to be well versed in computer science and has a lot of variety in specialties	

Team Management
Keeps everyone on target and manages tasks and goals, not necessarily a super game focused role but a very important one for any team

Concept Art
Makes art for the rest of the team to follow once ideas have been finalized since 2d sketches and renders are much cheaper and faster to produce than fully modelled, rigged, and animated characters

Visual Asset Creation
Makes the art that actually goes in the game, less creative than concept art but a creative role nonetheless

Sound
Produces the sound effects for the game, either from scratch by recording noises or pulling from sound libraries

Music
Makes the music for the game, often isn’t a full time team member, just an artist they hire	

Production
Manages the funds for the project as well and can also be a team lead

Marketing
Markets the game to publishers as well as potential players
	
Animation
Makes the animations for the game, can be a part of the art department

Game Programming Types
Architecture
Works on the core structure of the code, often requires a very deep understanding of computer science and works to optimize the code itself

UI
Programs how the UI functions, works heavily with UI design teams to create interfaces that are appealing and functional to the player

Physics
Programs the physics engine of the game and how physics objects interact. Varies in use depending on the game

Game Systems
Makes the systems for the game to actually run, functions like a layer above the architecture, actually focusing on the game itself, with other things like UI and Rendering above that

AI
Programs the AI algorithms for any procedural element of the game, AI can be from NPC pathing to random generation

Server
For an online game, makes the code for the game to interface with the internet and for people to be able to play together in some way

Rendering
Works on the graphics of the game, makes shaders and works with graphical APIs like Vulkan or OpenGL

Animation
Programs the animation made by the animation department into the game

Tools
Operates and creates tools for the programming team to use to streamline development

Sounds
	Programs in the sound of the game to play correctly
